{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>For he said: lest he die.</b> Rashi's explanation: she is established as one whose husbands die, as stated in Yevamot and Ketuvot: she was widowed twice, no longer fit to marry. And even according to the one who says she is not a 'killer wife' until three times, nevertheless he feared lest his seed be corrupted like his brothers and die, and the verse proves it: <b>lest he die like his brothers</b> — like the death of his brothers." "<b>Until Shelah grows up.</b> And he will be wise and guard himself from such a great sin. Another interpretation: <b>Remain a widow in your father's house until Shelah grows up</b> — and he will marry another woman and have sons from her, so that he not die without a male heir, and afterward he will perform levirate marriage with you. [The words 'בית אביך' are written defective, without a vav, as בית אביך.]"], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:07:53.399899268Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}